      "question": {
        ":question/id": "b58c5b26-0e3d-5bee-b269-b3dcb3172d92",
        ":question/problem": "Compute the following:\n\n| $\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 7 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 7 & 3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} |  |  |",
        ":question/worked-solution": "We multiply each row in the matrix by the column vector using the dot product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 7 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 7 & 3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{aligned}(-7)\\cdot 8 & + & 0\\cdot (-4) & + & 8\\cdot 1 \\\\ 7\\cdot 8 & + & 4\\cdot (-4) & + & 1\\cdot 1 \\\\ 7\\cdot 8 & + & 3\\cdot (-4) & + & (-2)\\cdot 1\\end{aligned}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}(-56) & + & 0 & + & 8 \\\\ 56 & + & (-16) & + & 1 \\\\ 56 & + & (-12) & + & (-2)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-48 \\\\ 41 \\\\ 42\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
